<h1>Terms of Use</h1>

<p>Welcome to the North Star Surrogacy (North Star Surrogacy) Portal. By creating an account, accessing, or using this portal, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Use ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms, do not access or use the portal.</p>

<h2>1. Portal Purpose</h2>
<p>The North Star Surrogacy Portal ("Portal") is a private, secure platform designed to facilitate communication, document management, and case tracking between North Star Surrogacy ("Agency," "we," "us," or "our") and its gestational carriers ("Surrogates"), intended parents ("IPs"), and their respective partners. The Portal is not a public website.</p>

<h2>2. Account Registration &amp; Security</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Surrogate Access:</strong> Surrogates who complete the intake qualification quiz and meet the Agency's preliminary screening criteria will automatically receive portal access with instructions to set their password.</li>
  <li><strong>Intended Parent &amp; Partner Access:</strong> Intended parents and their partners receive portal access by invitation from Agency staff. You will receive an email invitation with instructions to set your password.</li>
  <li><strong>Accurate Information:</strong> You agree to provide accurate, current, and complete information during the registration process and to update such information to keep it accurate.</li>
  <li><strong>Password Security:</strong> You are responsible for safeguarding your password and for all activities that occur under your account. You must notify the Agency immediately of any unauthorized use of your account.</li>
  <li><strong>One Account Per Person:</strong> Each account is for a single individual. Do not share your login credentials with anyone, including family members or partners (partners will receive their own invitation if applicable).</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Acceptable Use</h2>
<p>You agree to use the Portal only for its intended purpose — communicating with the Agency, managing your surrogacy journey, completing required forms, reviewing and signing documents, and accessing information related to your case. You agree NOT to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Share, distribute, or publicly post any content, documents, profiles, or personal information accessed through the Portal</li>
  <li>Attempt to access another user's account or any data not intended for you</li>
  <li>Use the Portal for any unlawful, harassing, discriminatory, or fraudulent purpose</li>
  <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract the source code of the Portal</li>
  <li>Upload malicious files, viruses, or harmful content</li>
  <li>Use automated tools, bots, or scrapers to access the Portal</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Confidentiality</h2>
<p>All information accessible through the Portal — including but not limited to surrogate profiles, intended parent profiles, medical information, legal documents, financial details, match information, and communications — is <strong>strictly confidential</strong>. You agree to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Treat all Portal content as confidential and proprietary</li>
  <li>Not disclose any information about other parties in your journey (surrogates, intended parents, partners, or Agency staff) to any third party without prior written consent</li>
  <li>Not screenshot, copy, download, or reproduce profiles or personal information of other parties except as expressly permitted by the Agency</li>
  <li>Maintain the confidentiality of any shared profiles, even after your journey concludes</li>
</ul>
<p>Breach of confidentiality may result in immediate account termination and may have legal consequences.</p>

<h2>5. Surrogacy-Specific Terms</h2>

<h3>5.1 Profile Information</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Profiles created on the Portal (surrogate matching profiles and intended parent profiles) are used solely for the purpose of facilitating matches between surrogates and intended parents through the Agency.</li>
  <li>You consent to the Agency sharing your profile with potential matches as part of the matching process.</li>
  <li>Profile information may include personal details, photos, health history, pregnancy history, and preferences. You represent that all information provided is truthful and accurate.</li>
  <li>The Agency reserves the right to approve, edit, or request changes to profiles before sharing.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.2 Medical Information</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The Portal may contain or reference sensitive medical information, including but not limited to: pregnancy history, medical evaluations, psychological evaluations, lab results, and insurance details.</li>
  <li>You acknowledge that this information is shared with the Agency and relevant parties (e.g., your case manager, attorneys, medical providers) as necessary to facilitate your surrogacy journey.</li>
  <li>The Agency is not a healthcare provider. Medical information in the Portal is for case management purposes only and does not constitute medical advice.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.3 Legal Documents &amp; E-Signatures</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The Portal includes electronic signature functionality for certain documents. By using the e-signature feature, you agree that your electronic signature is legally binding and has the same effect as a handwritten signature, in accordance with the federal ESIGN Act and applicable state laws.</li>
  <li>E-signed documents are stored securely and may be shared with attorneys, courts, or other parties as required by your surrogacy agreement.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.4 Financial Information</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The Portal may display escrow balances, expense tracking, insurance payment information, and compensation details. This information is provided for transparency and case management purposes.</li>
  <li>The Agency is not responsible for errors in third-party financial data (e.g., escrow company records). Please verify financial information with the relevant parties directly.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.5 No Guarantee of Match or Outcome</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Use of the Portal does not guarantee a surrogacy match, a successful pregnancy, or any particular outcome.</li>
  <li>The Agency reserves the right to decline or discontinue services at any time, in accordance with the terms of your separate surrogacy agreement.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
<p>All content, design, features, and functionality of the Portal are owned by North Star Surrogacy and are protected by copyright, trademark, and other intellectual property laws. You may not reproduce, distribute, or create derivative works based on the Portal without our express written permission.</p>

<h2>7. Privacy &amp; Data Protection</h2>
<p>Your privacy is important to us. Please review our <strong>Privacy Policy</strong> (below) for information about how we collect, use, store, and protect your personal information. By using the Portal, you consent to the collection and use of your information as described in the Privacy Policy.</p>

<h2>8. Account Termination &amp; Data Retention</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The Agency may suspend or terminate your account at any time, with or without cause, including but not limited to: completion of your journey, withdrawal from the program, breach of these Terms, or inactivity.</li>
  <li>Upon account termination, you will no longer have access to the Portal. Certain data may be retained as required by law, contractual obligations, or for legitimate business purposes.</li>
  <li>You may request deletion of your personal data by contacting the Agency, subject to legal and contractual retention requirements.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Limitation of Liability</h2>
<p class="caps">TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, ABC SURROGACY SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO LOSS OF DATA, LOSS OF PROFITS, OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO YOUR USE OF THE PORTAL.</p>
<p>The Portal is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, either express or implied. We do not warrant that the Portal will be uninterrupted, error-free, or secure.</p>

<h2>10. Indemnification</h2>
<p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless North Star Surrogacy, its officers, directors, employees, and agents from any claims, damages, losses, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of your use of the Portal, your violation of these Terms, or your violation of any rights of another party.</p>

<h2>11. Governing Law</h2>
<p>These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Texas, without regard to its conflict of law provisions. Any disputes arising under these Terms shall be resolved in the courts of Travis County, Texas.</p>

<h2>12. Changes to These Terms</h2>
<p>We reserve the right to update or modify these Terms at any time. If we make material changes, we will notify you through the Portal or via email. Your continued use of the Portal after such changes constitutes your acceptance of the updated Terms.</p>

<h2>13. Contact Us</h2>
<p>If you have questions about these Terms, please contact us at:</p>
<p><strong>North Star Surrogacy (North Star Surrogacy)</strong><br>
Email: info@northstarsurrogacy.com</p>

